; Opaque slot fixture: `:walk-opaque true` on a key whose value the
; surrounding schema types but does not read.
;
; `(template …)` holds a form the host expands later. Its body is
; unfinished on purpose: `(animate :from 0 :to 1)` has no `:target`
; because `(apply …)` supplies one at expansion time, and a body may
; use a head this plugin never declared, because the expansion runs
; under a different vocabulary. Neither is a mistake, and neither is
; something this schema can judge, so the slot is declared opaque.
;
; What opaque buys is exact, and it cuts both ways. The slot itself is
; still checked (`:type form`, so `:body 3` is `wrong_underlying`), and
; below the slot every walk stops, not only the validator's:
;
;   * no diagnostics inside: a missing required key or an undeclared
;     head in the body is not reported;
;   * no defaults inside: `animate`'s `:ease` default is never
;     materialized there, so `sjon effective` leaves the body alone;
;   * no cross-ref targets inside: an `(anchor :name x)` written in a
;     body registers nothing, so a reference to `x` misses;
;   * no lowering inside: a lowerable form in a body never fires its
;     hook.
;
; The third one is the reason to read `example-hidden-target.sjon`. It
; is the one way an opaque slot can add a diagnostic rather than
; suppress one, and it is the point of the flag: a subtree the schema
; declined to interpret is not a place to harvest names out of.
;
; The meta-schema uses the same flag on exactly one slot, the `(key …)`
; form's own `:default`, which is why a manifest can carry an
; expression-shaped default without the expression's head being
; reported as an unknown form.
;
; Schema export has nothing to say about the flag: the slot exports as
; a form-shaped slot like any other, because the exporters describe
; what a value may be and the flag is about what the validator reads.
;
; Each document beside this file is validated with the manifest
; prepended, which is also how the schema-export round-trip test reads
; them:
;
;   cat examples/plugins/opaque-slot/plugin.sjon \
;       examples/plugins/opaque-slot/example.sjon | sjon validate - --no-project
;
; and `sjon effective -` on the same pipe prints the effective view.

(plugin :name template :version "1.0.0"
  :description "Reference plugin for `:walk-opaque`: a slot the schema types and does not read."

  (value-kind :name ease
    :description "The easing curve names the host knows."
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [linear ease-in ease-out]))

  (value-kind :name anchor-name
    :description "Cross-ref to an `(anchor :name …)` the document declares."
    :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target anchor))

  (value-kind :name template-name
    :description "Cross-ref to a `(template :name …)` the document declares."
    :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target template))

  (form :name anchor
    :description "A named point an animation can target."
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name animate
    :description "A finished animation. Every key is checked when this form is written at the top level."
    (key :name target :type anchor-name :optional false)
    (key :name from :type number :optional false)
    (key :name to :type number :optional false)
    (key :name ease :type ease :optional true :default linear))

  (form :name template
    :description "A named body the host expands later. `:body` is typed `form` and read by nobody here."
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false)
    (key :name body :type form :optional false :walk-opaque true
      :description "Opaque: the slot is a form, and what is inside it is the expander's business."))

  (form :name apply
    :description "Expand a template against a target."
    (key :name template :type template-name :optional false)
    (key :name target :type anchor-name :optional false)))
